Staged patches: verified on the host, waiting for their own flight
==================================================================

Files here are NOT applied by scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh (its glob is
kernel/patches/*.patch). They are promoted into the series (moved up one
directory, with their config fragment moved from kernel/config/staged/ to
kernel/config/) when the flight before them has passed, so that each RAM
boot carries one variable.

0056-0062 — the OnePlus Pad 4 pen charger (Maxic MT5806 wireless power
transmitter on the magnet edge, which charges the Stylo Pro), from the
Fedora iceland port (author mzak), with the three prerequisites its
dependency audit found our tree lacked:
  0056/0057  PMH0101 level shifters ls1-ls4 as RPMh XOB regulators
             (binding + driver; the board only instantiates ls3/ls4,
             which gate the I2C hub bus the charger sits on)
  0058       a pmic_glink "hboost" auxiliary device on this board's
             compatible (oplus,kaanapali-pmic-glink) — the client that asks
             the charger firmware for the hBoost converter voltage
  0059-0061  binding, driver (drivers/power/supply/mt5806_pen_charger.c)
             and the board DT node (I2C hub bus 1 @0x2b, IRQ gpio169, four
             PMIH0108 control lines, 7 V idle / 10 V charging)
  0062       the first s2idle after load must not be aborted by the IC's
             post-start interrupt (Fedora 0179)
Config: kernel/config/staged/config-pen-charger.fragment (=m).
Verified: all seven apply as files after 0001-0055 (and after 0001-0039);
mt5806_pen_charger.o, pmic_glink.o and qcom-rpmh-regulator.o compile with
0 warnings (W=1 too); the DTB carries the node with all five pinctrl
states resolving and the touchscreen node intact. Gate and risks:
docs/bringup-plan.md A.3b.
